Q: Sort on enum field using different sort orders A: <p>If you create a dictionary for the sort order, you can use that for fast conversion from the enum to a sorting order:</p>

<pre><code>Dictionary&lt;enume, int&gt; sort = new Dictionary&lt;enume, int&gt;();
sort.Add(enume.support, 0);
sort.Add(enume.defensive, 1);
sort.Add(enume.offensive, 2);
</code></pre>

<p>Now just sort on the conversion:</p>

<pre><code>List&lt;Item&gt; result = items.OrderBy(i =&gt; sort[i.enume]).ToList();
</code></pre>

<p>To sort the enum values in a different way, just put the values in the dictionary with different numbers:</p>

<pre><code>sort.Add(enume.offensive, 0);
sort.Add(enume.support, 1);
sort.Add(enume.defensive, 2);
</code></pre>

